# Vector illustrations for understanding

When building or improving user-facing flows (onboarding, dashboards, empty states, benefit/responsibility explainers, success moments), **generate simple visual vector illustrations** when they help the user understand faster than text alone.

## Prefer

- Theme-aware SVG components under `src/components/illustrations/` (or `src/components/feedback/` for celebratory moments)
- `react-native-svg` shapes (`Circle`, `Rect`, `Path`) using `useTheme()` colors — no hardcoded brand hex unless dynamic contrast requires it
- One clear metaphor per illustration (e.g. store → coin for commission; two people for accompaniment)
- Accessible wrappers: `accessibilityRole="image"` and a short `accessibilityLabel`
- Keep illustrations small and focused (~96–160px); place above the related headline

## Avoid

- Generic stock photos or emoji as the primary teaching visual
- Dense decorative art that competes with copy
- Skipping an illustration when the concept is abstract (commissions, referrals, moderation, verification)

## Example placement

Explainers (benefit / responsibility / how-it-works) should pair each section with a short illustration + title + one supporting sentence.
